# Research Notebook MCP — R&D discipline

This repo targets **notebook-style research** with an LLM. When using or implementing the MCP server, favour **understanding over polish**.

- **Look at real data**: samples, plots on disk, **stderr** alongside stdout. Metrics alone are not enough.
- Trace **data flow** and **middle states**—not only final outputs. Prefer **`notebook_outline`** (cell ids/sources), **`run`** payloads (streams, previews, errors), and **`variable_preview`** (capped **`repr`** of plain names in **`globals()`**—no dotted lookups) plus disk reads—not chat-only guesses.
- **Debug** with kernel truth: respect **stale-output** hints and **`kernel_generation`** after restarts; rerun chains when diagnosing.
- Use **`dry_run`** to resolve the same selectors as **`run`** without executing when ids or companion alignment are unclear; call **`notebook_outline`** before **`run(..., cell_id=…)`** when ids are unknown.
- **Keep cell logic compact**—few toy abstractions—not comment-free prose. **Comment and narrate generously** in **`#`** lines or Markdown cells: hypotheses, why this step follows the last **`run`**, what surprised you (`stderr`/plots), forks you tried—R&D notebooks should read like a lab log when chat history is gone.
- Prefer **`notebook_cells_patch`** / **`cells_apply`** (structured edits by **`metadata.cell_id`**) **or validated companion mirrors** (**`.apynb`** / **`export-apynb --format yaml`**) over hand-editing raw `.ipynb` JSON.

